      "id": "tp-split",
      "title": "Estimate tensor-parallel splits before loading",
      "claims": [
        {
          "text": "TPAllocation describes replicated and shardable storage, replicated and shardable overhead, reconstruction workspace, and a logical partition axis. Module.make_tp_allocation concatenates records in registered-child order. The sequential and parallel transformer blocks inherit that traversal. Embedding and PosEmbedding return no records; Conv explicitly raises. Mistral3PatchMerger can recurse into its registered Linear, while Gemma3MMPool is a childless module without an override.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_368480094ac744c1a77bf577252332a6", "call_d976daf7c93a40c5887029982d217a84", "call_4543e2c9dc604c8d816c6adb72fcb4f1", "call_5330001a85e844349488c8128b490762", "call_4bc53cb24fa64870a9dc57ed8db2a4d9", "call_f390d4cde2614cfa9ff6f6d37260ebe6", "call_67fb9722df794eefa84da01322fb313c", "call_171e4e7e96b949ac99f85b06e6a47af8", "call_5140e8227cef41b282ebbeb5ce31a805", "call_c648f6b600d44d76bd62cedb1ab9c258"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Linear caches the primary-key storage estimate: an EXL3 group requires trellis plus one form each of the input and output scales; the estimator then sums tensor byte sizes under that prefix. Otherwise, storage and reconstruction each use two bytes per element of the padded matrix, not a measurement of a loaded tensor or a bias-inclusive FP16 count. The same header-size API already served conversion shard packing and Model.get_storage_info. LayerNorm and RMSNorm count their prefix bytes as replicated storage and estimate one output row as floor(storage_bytes/2) times output item size; this is a proxy, not a lookup of the actual normalized width.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_7c3b30d7166c431fbc034cad7047c25b", "call_dd4a2551406543cbade106ae6b0c64c0", "call_a2f85e8e9f3347c296cd3d265c104d0c", "call_2d85d18af20645c0b614a6e34cdedf71", "call_b41605de767145a696cad53e7520c0da", "call_c371ef742b434e86aa4fc2f4abbda292", "call_4eb2b81a95564ed3ba1abfee0e1baea6", "call_4a4a9841086147018062aca8e3fd7fe5"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Attention groups four projection estimates and every attached cache under the attn limit, splitting by whole KV heads. It charges a replicated hidden-width output, two half-width query-head vectors for Q/O and two half-width KV-head vectors for K/V, plus cache overhead. Reconstruction is the maximum of the four projection estimates. FP16 cache storage is two full-capacity half tensors, with no separate reconstruction buffer; quantized storage is two packed int32 payloads with independently sized K/V bitplanes and two FP16 scale arrays, one scale per 32 values per tensor. Quantized get_kv allocates just one pair of full-capacity half tensors per call.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_92dd2016fccb439a8149f064e04804e5", "call_c2bb255d10564de08629052798670d65", "call_1e944e009be54fd3a85f9f5e5eea9046", "call_8b83a1af6f9644c2a6e9000d6c5d3e6a", "call_83c3c71a5aa84315bcea984e19661abf", "call_d39c35ac8ad7416eb065daec98440baf"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Standalone Linear partitions padded output width in 128-channel blocks; plain MLP uses that granularity for intermediate width and combines up/down storage. GatedMLP combines all gate/up/down storage, charges two intermediate vectors plus an extra half vector when interm_dtype is not half, and switches from 128-channel chunks to existing slices for an already sliced module. The existing slicer aligns the base slice width to 128 and leaves the remainder in the last slice. The planner still prices slices uniformly and uses only the first slice's projections for the reconstruction bound; its display multiplies slice counts by 128 as well. BlockSparseMLP instead uses one expert per unit, includes the router in the split storage total, budgets four intermediate vectors plus the conditional half vector, and appends a separate estimate for any shared experts.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_dd4a2551406543cbade106ae6b0c64c0", "call_7c3b30d7166c431fbc034cad7047c25b", "call_1f3b3a2bbfb44cebaa88c7e6b2de3491", "call_1b95029705b04de48dff21728d99a8cd", "call_e9d34090519443fcb3bc67944fc5fb92", "call_885ad170e7d94c52bde72b516f0c9c0e", "call_368480094ac744c1a77bf577252332a6"]
        },
        {
          "text": "initial_split walks components in order. It subtracts accumulated storage and peak overhead from each budget, clips negative room to zero, and optionally keeps only the devices with the most remaining room using the component limit or a dev_limits override. ratio_split gets unit-sized chunks, floors each nonnegative proportional quota, and gives leftovers to the largest fractional remainders. The planner adds the replicated charges on positive-room devices and prorates the split charges by each rounded share using integer division. Only split overhead gets the token multiplier, using output_num_tokens for the final component object and num_tokens otherwise. compile_tp_plan turns the splits into consecutive half-open logical ranges per device and key, including empty ranges; only print_split scales the counts by channel_width, and its label 'GB' uses a GiB divisor.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_2ee6dc3b4f734965bbde6924c5473cff", "call_368480094ac744c1a77bf577252332a6"]
        },
        {
          "text": "A standard-library transcription gave 4,194,304 bytes of FP16 K/V storage at 1,024 cache tokens, eight KV heads and head width 128. Four-bit keys and six-bit values used 1,441,792 persistent bytes plus the same 4,194,304-byte FP16 reconstruction pair. Applying the planner's token multiplier to that pair alone for eight forward tokens on one device gives 33,554,432 estimated bytes.",
          "basis": "execution",
          "evidence": ["call_c421c73f513d4f1d8e044fece19f697a", "call_9cc392da195d494d9eb82afcb74c4f85"]
        }
      ]
    }
